        <FontName>Arial</FontName>
        <TextLines>
          <TextLine>Specialist-MX2 / SCART RGB adapter</TextLine>
        </TextLines>
      </Shape>
      <Shape Type="Text" Id="53" Sheet="0" Angle="0" HorzAlign="Left" VertAlign="Top" TextAlign="Left" FontVector="Y" FontSize="8" FontWidth="-2" FontScale="1" FontColor="0" LineSpacing="1.2">
        <Points>
          <Point X="600" Y="5550" />
        </Points>
        <FontName>Arial</FontName>
        <TextLines>
          <TextLine>XP1: IDC-10 to ram-slots XP19 (1:1); H/V on pins 8/9 through existing 470 ohm. SCART cable to TV.</TextLine>
        </TextLines>
      </Shape>
      <Shape Type="Text" Id="54" Sheet="0" Angle="0" HorzAlign="Left" VertAlign="Top" TextAlign="Left" FontVector="Y" FontSize="8" FontWidth="-2" FontScale="1" FontColor="0" LineSpacing="1.2">
        <Points>
          <Point X="600" Y="800" />
        </Points>
        <FontName>Arial</FontName>
        <TextLines>
          <TextLine>D1/D2: cathodes to H/V, anodes joined at CSYNC_RAW. R4/R5 form a 4.7k + 4.7k bias divider.</TextLine>
          <TextLine>Keep ram-slots 470 ohm resistors and specialist-m R9. No added wire to IDC pin 6.</TextLine>
          <TextLine>Q1 buffers the sum; R1/R2 attenuation = 0.1875 into 75 ohm. SCART 19 -&gt; cable -&gt; TV 20.</TextLine>
          <TextLine>REV2 REVIEW DRAFT: native DipTrace ERC/DRC and hardware levels not yet verified.</TextLine>
        </TextLines>
      </Shape>
